{"type":"message","id":"040451ef","parentId":"09e7c1f3","timestamp":"2026-03-18T13:00:33.658Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Explaining routing issues**\n\nI’m considering how to explain a likely routing issue briefly. It seems like I need to identify the symptoms of the problem and any common causes. I'll make sure to keep it clear and concise so that it’s understandable. For instance, I might touch on issues like packet loss or connectivity problems. I want to provide the user with the information they need without overwhelming them. Let's keep it focused!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_007ee785528742940169baa1ed41f88191a67b647a0e63468c\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpuqHvpfmJLYrCcKt3aSsnuODCf3AIh-t6ZUodFDioFBzHX9IUXNTB35-2likpXk85WtFaGLm3wDY4PCARJc0r6TjiO3PNdQm-qXCJLaQkot3-gm6R02twJQbiBgM2hrRrBRNauUeu8vDPfXb76zG3qAVTaX6SjITMrfMzea2rHZ6bsWEAO-sr3UEOcS-kZBwzIuRIZoNwn9PFaN5o06eb1bh8alxNgL_jsX_AlESklGdigMxhONZUk_ZMyTqO9jxbwgoiabiyQm7ZC_1HUNl7lP2LRiMv5ss3tbcRU8qNuEWJNtzHDbPBtA5IdKxFDVWmW6NdH6yOSGKaHSmQmMNSlYLAsumvvBWVZMo_idrqs_uJRRvo1kHtKyDFbhULVl_w2JMy_uUgTyw9d6Cg-PVlTT4ZK3PJR43Zu25fXvxaMZ5gl4YQR-3OTXiD9Fms1ntWpIDJT3S_PZmDReeZ8tSqZAVtUf7WBobUBhLikopNw66fcOk8IqAhx6e4vK-QpjN7ZAOKoFLQqOV2XRfhXN6PEYAKNzP5skOM75M7h4CABENmlo2kablkK_jKVzizWGZaV01ZMVjjQTsnbFpGqia5WWvJYLsfrgdrAhPm1hepDA1DxSgOffMOjKc292zQ0MziQfo3mdskmLnVq1PIU64eYlb5B34LB9z6LF4ITUd67BPNA3m0jmj9keXGg7AQeFkJf5i6CSUpCDZzi4Pxe3N_Kjg1I8QBTqo5gmT99cA9mq_kNwT1q4EuEIY_Gs6PtGaZU196syAPEBj428hwAO9pQ55d7kV14D-ke-1LO4846B5a9ZZBDK9gwUkBEnqGeobCsMzETzQspcoUXwVkR8mbE8urjLvRf7uC1lQo25mHDDadIAiAJmGzoxoAx7_Ofxu7jg3a\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Explaining routing issues**\\n\\nI’m considering how to explain a likely routing issue briefly. It seems like I need to identify the symptoms of the problem and any common causes. I'll make sure to keep it clear and concise so that it’s understandable. For instance, I might touch on issues like packet loss or connectivity problems. I want to provide the user with the information they need without overwhelming them. Let's keep it focused!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Most likely because the pipeline script tried to send the image as a separate Telegram media message through the CLI, and that send appears to have reported success internally, but delivery did not actually show up in the chat.\n\nThat can happen when:\n- the script sends the image as a second outbound message rather than attaching it to my reply\n- Telegram/provider delivery succeeds only partially or silently fails after the local send step\n- the returned file is in a format/content-type combination that the transport accepts inconsistently\n\nWhen I resent it as `MEDIA:./kidney-heatmap.jpeg` in the chat reply itself, it used the native reply path for this conversation, which is usually more reliable here. If you want, I can from now on send result images only inline with my reply instead of relying on the pipeline’s separate send step.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_007ee785528742940169baa1efdb708191ae00ddec5bb37a00\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":432,"output":190,"cacheRead":22272,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22894,"cost":{"input":0.00108,"output":0.00285,"cacheRead":0.005568,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.009498}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773838825997}}
