ng that the issue is fixed. It could be helpful to include media to demonstrate the fix visually. Since the user asked for a skill fix, I think I should output an image each time from now on. It might be good to confirm that I will ensure to attach an image inline whenever necessary. Now, I’ll figure out how to include that image through the MEDIA path.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Fixed — I changed the kidney-pipeline-execution skill so it no longer relies on a separate Telegram send step.\n\n**What changed**\n- The script now always downloads the analyzer image and writes a **reply-ready copy** into the workspace.\n- The skill now instructs the agent to attach that image **in the same reply** using the native media path, which is the most straightforward and reliable method here.\n- I tested the updated script end-to-end on your image, and it now returns:\n  - `reply_media_path`\n  - `reply_media_name`\n\nSo from now on, when the pipeline produces an output image, I can send it directly in the same answer like this:\n\nMEDIA:./kidney-pipeline-last-heatmap.jpeg\n\nIf you want, I can also make one more improvement: have the skill explicitly fail loudly when no analyzer image is produced, instead of silently returning only text.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_007ee785528742940169baa2879e1481919a4793b1d8f4024c\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9826,"output":242,"cacheRead":38784,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":48852,"cost":{"input":0.024565000000000003,"output":0.00363,"cacheRead":0.009696,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.03789100000000001}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773838978099}}
